{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1aG2wMetcUfr"},"source":["*Benjamin Bradley*\n","\n","**Date: March 13th, 2024**\n","\n","In this colab I hope to be build off my work in [240306 Ben Bradley - Developing the Models](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1Y2D7bha8J5FA_0NGNNK835vi0FzDvMdc#scrollTo=3JdGl-YMDiAS) where I experimented with Hardcoded Heuristics, PID Solutions, Q-Learning, many weeks of DQN implementations, and settled on a Actor-Critic model as the most appealling model to move forward with. I ran into the problem of [*Fluctuating Performance of DQNs*](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1711.07478.pdf) which caused my DQN to get stuck in a plateau of performance ~350 steps per round (out of a 500 step maximum), indicating the fraility of DQNs for reliable Cartpole-V1 policies. I observed good performance for simple $\\dot \\theta + \\theta$ policies and outstanding performance for simple PID solutions.\n","\n","In this Colab I:\n","- Experimented with the space state through decreasing the x-bounds (hopefully leading the models to caring about x drift more).\n","- Explained further the mechanics of Actor-Critic models.\n","- Maximized and prodded at the degree of Actor-Critic Effectiveness.\n","- Achieve a basic continuous (aka Analog) action space on the Cartpole-V1 game.\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Vi_Kwv9-GmgR"},"source":["## Actor-Critic Architecture & Training Loop\n","\n","Actor-Critic models have said name because they integrate two sub-models into one:\n","\n","- An Actor Model which learns the optimal policy $\\pi(a_t|s_t)$ aka which action to take given a state\n","- A Critic model which learns to estimate the value $V(s)$ of different states in a way not disimilar to DQNs\n","\n","For a Actor-Critic model to \"learn\" therefore means to adjust the Actor's policy parameters in order to ascend the gradient of policy rewards with respect to the Critic's value estimates. This is a combination of Policy-learning and Value-learning which optimally allows the policy to be learned quicker and the value to be more reflective of reality through using the information in both models concurrently to explore the possible action space.\n","\n","\n","> $R_t = r_t + γR_{t-1}$ \\\\\n","\n","> $A_t=R_t-V(s_t)$ \\\\\n","\n","> $L_{actor}=-\\sum \\text{ } \\log(\\pi (a_t | s_t)) \\cdot A_t$ \\\\\n","\n","> $L_{critic}=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum \\text{ } (R_t-V(s_t)^2)$"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"uTQZq3B5qnLo"},"source":["### Architecture"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ew0_hj3K6IqR"},"source":["![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"vDu-mlSxcITZ"},"outputs":[],"source":["import gym\n","from gym import spaces\n","import time\n","import math\n","import numpy as np\n","import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","import torch.optim as optim\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from matplotlib import animation\n","from IPython.display import HTML\n","\n","class Actor(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self, state_size, action_size, hidden_size=24):\n","        super(Actor, self).__init__()\n","        self.network = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Linear(state_size, hidden_size),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.Linear(hidden_size, action_size),\n","            nn.Softmax(dim=-1)\n","        )\n","\n","    def forward(self, state):\n","        return self.network(state)\n","\n","class Critic(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self, state_size, hidden_size=24):\n","        super(Critic, self).__init__()\n","        self.network = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Linear(state_size, hidden_size),\n","            nn.ReLU(),\n","            nn.Linear(hidden_size, 1)\n","        )\n","\n","    def forward(self, state):\n","        return self.network(state)\n","\n","def test_run(env, actor, num_test_episodes=100):\n","    total_rewards = []\n","    for i in range(num_test_episodes):\n","        state = env.reset()\n","        done = False\n","        episode_reward = 0\n","        while not done:\n","            state = torch.FloatTensor(state).unsqueeze(0)\n","            with torch.no_grad():\n","                probs = actor(state)\n","                action = probs.max(1)[1].view(1, 1)\n","            next_state, reward, done, _ = env.step(action.item())\n","            episode_reward += reward\n","            state = next_state\n","        total_rewards.append(episode_reward)\n","        print(f\"\\t Total Rewards = {total_rewards}\", end=\"\")\n","    average_reward = np.mean(total_rewards)\n","    print(f\"\\nAverage Testing Reward: {average_reward}\")\n","    return average_reward\n","\n","def train(env, actor, actor_filename, critic, critic_filename, actor_optimizer, critic_optimizer, max_steps=500, n_episodes=1000, gamma=0.99):\n","    start_time = time.time()\n","    all_rewards = []\n","    all_actor_losses = []\n","    all_critic_losses = []\n","    old_rew = 0\n","    for episode in range(n_episodes):\n","        state = env.reset()\n","        done = False\n","        log_probs = []\n","        values = []\n","        rewards = []\n","        episode_reward = 0\n","\n","        # Play through one episode\n","        while not done:\n","            state = torch.FloatTensor(state).unsqueeze(0)\n","            probs = actor(state)\n","            value = critic(state)\n","            dist = torch.distributions.Categorical(probs)\n","            action = dist.sample()\n","\n","            next_state, reward, done, _ = env.step(action.item())\n","            episode_reward += reward\n","\n","            log_probs.append(dist.log_prob(action)) # Prob of our action\n","            values.append(value) # Value Critic assigned to the current state\n","            rewards.append(torch.tensor([reward], dtype=torch.float)) # Reward of next state\n","\n","            state = next_state\n","\n","        # Calculate adjusted returns of all the starts based on length of episode\n","        returns = []\n","        all_rewards.append(episode_reward)\n","        R = 0\n","        for r in reversed(rewards):\n","            R = r + gamma * R\n","            returns.insert(0, R)\n","\n","        returns = torch.cat(returns).detach()\n","        log_probs = torch.cat(log_probs)\n","        values = torch.cat(values)\n","\n","        advantage = returns - values # Diff b/w Critics expected Value and actual adjusted Value\n","\n","        # Adjust for loss\n","        actor_loss = -(log_probs * advantage.detach()).mean() # Descend loss where loss = confidence in action * how far the expected value was from actual adjusted value to adjust actor model\n","        critic_loss = advantage.pow(2).mean() # MSE of difference to adjust critic model\n","\n","        all_actor_losses.append(actor_loss.item())\n","        all_critic_losses.append(critic_loss.item())\n","\n","        actor_optimizer.zero_grad()\n","        critic_optimizer.zero_grad()\n","\n","        actor_loss.backward()\n","        critic_loss.backward()\n","\n","        actor_optimizer.step()\n","        critic_optimizer.step()\n","\n","        # Print Episode #, Loss, and Test Reward\n","        print('\\rEpisode {}\\t Actor Loss: {:.2f} Critic Loss {:.2f} \\t Episode Reward {}' \\\n","          .format(episode, actor_loss.item(), critic_loss.item(), episode_reward), end=\"\")\n","        if episode % 100 == 0 and episode != 0:\n","            print('\\rEpisode {}\\t Avg Loss: {:.2f} \\t Avg Episode Reward {}' \\\n","              .format(episode, np.mean(all_actor_losses[-100:]), np.mean(all_critic_losses[-100:]), np.mean(all_rewards[-100:])), end=\"\")\n","\n","        if episode % 50 == 0:\n","            avg_rew = test_run(env, actor)\n","            if avg_rew == max_steps and old_rew == max_steps:\n","              break\n","            old_rew = avg_rew\n","\n","    avg_rew = test_run(env, actor)\n","    time_taken = time.time() - start_time\n","    print(f\"\\n---- TRAINING DONE IN {round(time_taken, 2)} SECONDS ----\")\n","    print(\" \")\n","\n","    torch.save(actor.state_dict(), actor_filename)\n","    torch.save(critic.state_dict(), critic_filename)\n","\n","    return all_rewards, all_losses, time_taken"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"w2iIy5qcfpbp"},"outputs":[],"source":["def trainModel(env, hidden_size, lr, max_steps, n_episodes, actor_filename, critic_filepath):\n","    state_size = 4\n","    action_size = 2\n","\n","    actor = Actor(state_size, action_size, hidden_size=hidden_size)\n","    critic = Critic(state_size, hidden_size=hidden_size)\n","\n","    actor_optimizer = optim.Adam(actor.parameters(), lr=lr)\n","    critic_optimizer = optim.Adam(critic.parameters(), lr=lr)\n","\n","    all_rewards, all_losses, time_taken = train(env, actor, actor_filename, critic, critic_filepath, actor_optimizer, critic_optimizer, max_steps, n_episodes)\n","\n","    return all_rewards, all_losses, time_taken, actor\n","\n","def moving_average(data, window_size):\n","    \"\"\"Calculate the moving average of the given list.\"\"\"\n","    i = 0\n","    moving_averages = []\n","\n","    while i < len(data) - window_size + 1:\n","        window_average = round(np.sum(data[\n","          i:i+window_size]) / window_size, 2)\n","        moving_averages.append(window_average)\n","        i += 1\n","\n","    return moving_averages\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Function to add an arrow to the frame\n","def add_arrow(frame, action):\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n","    ax.imshow(frame)\n","    ax.set_axis_off()\n","    arrow_props = dict(facecolor='black', edgecolor='black', arrowstyle='->', lw=3)\n","    if action == 0:  # Left\n","        ax.annotate('', xy=(0.05, 0.1), xytext=(0.15, 0.1), xycoords='axes fraction', arrowprops=arrow_props)\n","    else:  # Right\n","        ax.annotate('', xy=(0.15, 0.1), xytext=(0.05, 0.1), xycoords='axes fraction', arrowprops=arrow_props)\n","    fig.canvas.draw()\n","    frame_with_arrow = np.array(fig.canvas.renderer.buffer_rgba())\n","    plt.close(fig)\n","    return frame_with_arrow\n","\n","# Animation function\n","def animate(frames, actions):\n","    frames = [add_arrow(frame, action) for frame, action in zip(frames, actions)]\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n","    ax.set_axis_off()\n","    ims = [[plt.imshow(frame, animated=True, interpolation='none')] for frame in frames]\n","\n","    ani = animation.ArtistAnimation(fig, ims, interval=50, blit=True, repeat_delay=1000)\n","    plt.close()\n","    return HTML(ani.to_jshtml())"],"metadata":{"id":"N4GzBI8IvFCH"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### History"],"metadata":{"id":"ENwZefq2UCK9"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Lq6XvRKL3DoV"},"outputs":[],"source":["# TRAINING TIME / PERFORM FOR HIDDEN LAYER SIZES (2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024)\n","\n","# --- D= 2 ---\n","# Episode 0\t Loss: 5.52\tAverage Testing Reward: 12.4\n","# Episode 50\t Loss: 4.80\tAverage Testing Reward: 15.6\n","# Episode 100\t Loss: 3.32\tAverage Testing Reward: 24.4\n","# Episode 150\t Loss: 4.41\tAverage Testing Reward: 33.0\n","# Episode 200\t Loss: 7.25\tAverage Testing Reward: 43.0\n","# Episode 250\t Loss: 14.26\tAverage Testing Reward: 136.4\n","# Episode 300\t Loss: 11.26\tAverage Testing Reward: 262.8\n","# Episode 350\t Loss: 5.36\tAverage Testing Reward: 1713.6\n","# Episode 400\t Loss: 22.32\tAverage Testing Reward: 396.6\n","# Episode 450\t Loss: 23.67\tAverage Testing Reward: 1220.2\n","# Episode 500\t Loss: 30.04\tAverage Testing Reward: 3335.8\n","# Episode 550\t Loss: 15.45\tAverage Testing Reward: 1310.4\n","# Episode 600\t Loss: 13.59\tAverage Testing Reward: 15000.0\n","# \tAverage Testing Reward: 15000.0\n","\n","# ---- TRAINING DONE IN 153.8 SECONDS ----\n","\n","# --- D= 4 ---\n","# Episode 0\t Loss: 12.24\tAverage Testing Reward: 9.4\n","# Episode 50\t Loss: 7.55\tAverage Testing Reward: 9.0\n",