d: 4440.4\n","# Episode 250\t Loss: -0.03\tAverage Testing Reward: 15000.0\n","# \tAverage Testing Reward: 15000.0\n","\n","# ---- TRAINING DONE IN 1854.93 SECONDS ----"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Observing a learned policy of Stable Oscillation\n","\n","First we will train a Actor Critic model with a hidden_layer size of 32, a maximum number of 15000 timesteps per episode, and which cuts off training after two 100 episodes periods of 15000 timesteps being reached sepearted *or* after 5000 episodes of training.\n","\n","While training we will adjust the x range to $[-1,1]$ in order to try and encourage the model to learn to adjust for x coordinate drift in a way which wide x ranges does not.\n","\n","To adjust the x range, max number of timesteps, and size of frames to be rendered we will reference the [source code](https://github.com/openai/gym/blob/master/gym/envs/classic_control/cartpole.py) of Cartpole-V1 game.\n","\n","The following code shows:\n","- Training that model (attached is a plot of that trainings reward over time)\n","- Measuring that model over a single 1,000 step episode\n","- Measuring that model 50 times in terms of x-coordinate on 10,000 step episodes to test for susceptability to breaking the x bounds\n","\n","All of which offer promising results.\n","\n","The following chart shows rewards of the model over the course of 30k episodes of training over the course of just over 2 hours of training..."],"metadata":{"id":"O9nSz9HzQeiM"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"V5-EQWSC5UWf"},"source":["![Screenshot 2024-03-22 at 6.21.07 PM.png](data:image/png;base64,)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":12375001,"status":"ok","timestamp":1710992831227,"user":{"displayName":"Benjamin Bradley","userId":"04603304923366878970"},"user_tz":240},"id":"Gmq9xDZBMEj6","outputId":"eb6dd795-e774-467c-bfac-06fee7e2f401"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"strea